{
  "uid": "compliance-platform",
  "title": "Compliance Platform — Overview",
  "description": "The one dashboard P3.5 called for. Ordered by the question an operator asks first: is anything down, is data safe, and what do the logs say. Panel descriptions cite the measurement behind each threshold — hover the (i) rather than guessing why a number is what it is.",
  "tags": [
    "compliance",
    "platform",
    "p3.5"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "editable": false,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "Prometheus",
          "value": "Prometheus"
        },
        "hide": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "DS_LOKI",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "loki",
        "current": {
          "text": "Loki",
          "value": "Loki"
        },
        "hide": 2
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Service health — is anything down?",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Health endpoints",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "probe_success{probe_kind=\"health\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Every service's own /health, probed from outside the container. Each endpoint is deliberately shallow — it reports on its own process and does not probe its upstreams, because a check that reaches a wedged upstream inherits the wedge. This panel is where the whole-stack picture is composed instead.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "The two silent failures: ActiveMQ and Solr",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "probe_success{probe_kind=~\"broker|search\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "These get their own panel because neither fails loudly. FOOTPRINT_AUDIT.md measured that a dead ActiveMQ fails nothing synchronously — Alfresco keeps answering and specific operations hang forever with no error — and that a dead Solr hangs the gateway while the Web Scripts fail cleanly. Both are TCP probes: ActiveMQ's web console can be up while its broker transport is not, and Solr sits behind shared-secret comms that answer 401 whether it is healthy or not.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "UNREACHABLE",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "OK",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Health probe latency",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "probe_duration_seconds{probe_kind=\"health\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "These endpoints do no I/O beyond their own process, so a healthy one answers in milliseconds. A rising line here is usually the early shape of a hang, which is this platform's characteristic failure — it shows up as latency before it shows up as an outage.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Container memory against its limit",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "container_memory_working_set_bytes{container!=\"\"} / (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{container!=\"\"} > 0)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{container}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Fraction of each container's declared limit in use. Read this with the measured baseline in mind: FOOTPRINT_AUDIT.md found Alfresco idling at 95–97% of its cap in normal operation, so a line near the top is not automatically a problem here. The alert threshold is 98% sustained for 15 minutes for exactly that reason.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1.2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Data safety — backups, WAL and disk",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "WAL archiving",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "pg_archiver_failing",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{database}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Whether archiving is working NOW — the last attempt failed and none has succeeded since — rather than a cumulative failure count. Counters survive restarts, so a count-based view stays red forever after one transient blip and stops being read. When this goes red, PostgreSQL retains every WAL segment until archiving recovers and the volume fills until the database stops.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "OK",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "FAILING",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "WAL archiving backlog",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 14
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "pg_archiver_ready_count",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{database}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "WAL segments PostgreSQL has marked ready that the archive_command has not consumed. A healthy archiver drains these in seconds, so anything sustained here is a stall — and every queued segment is occupying the data volume until it clears. Watched instead of the age of the last archive, because archive_timeout does not force a segment switch on a database that has written no WAL: an idle database archives nothing, correctly, and an age-based panel reads as broken every quiet weekend.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Databases",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 14
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "pg_up",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{database}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "All three PostgreSQL instances: AtroCore's, Alfresco's, and compliance_web's.",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Free disk space",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "node_filesystem_avail_bytes{fstype!~\"tmpfs|overlay|squashfs\"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{fstype!~\"tmpfs|overlay|squashfs\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{mountpoint}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Watched more closely than the platform's size would suggest, because of what fills it: retained WAL from a failing archiver, and the Alfresco content store. Neither stops on its own, and PostgreSQL stops when the disk does.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Container CPU",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{container!=\"\"}[5m])",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{container}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Cores in use per container. FOOTPRINT_AUDIT.md's floor is 4–8 vCPU for the platform alone.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Authentication",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Logins per second",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_success_total[5m])",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "success"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_failed_total[5m])",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_rate_limited_total[5m])",
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "rate-limited"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_provider_unavailable_total[5m])",
          "refId": "D",
          "legendFormat": "Alfresco unreachable"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The first two metrics from AUTH_CHUNK8 §6. Rate-limited attempts and Alfresco outages are counted separately from failures on purpose: a rate-limited attempt never reached the credential check, and an outage is not a wrong password — folding either into the failure count would make a brute-force attempt or an IdP outage read as a user problem.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Role-cache refresh failure share",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_role_refresh_failed_total[10m]) / (rate(auth_role_refresh_failed_total[10m]) + rate(auth_role_refresh_success_total[10m]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "failure share"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Metric 6, and the quietest failure in the auth system. When Alfresco is unreachable the session survives on cached roles for a grace period, so nobody notices — until the grace period ends and every user loses their permissions at once. Shown as a share rather than a count because the absolute number scales with how many people are logged in.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Session 401s, CSRF mismatches and rotations",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_session_401_total[5m])",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "session 401"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_csrf_mismatch_total[5m])",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "CSRF mismatch"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(auth_session_rotated_total[5m])",
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "session rotated"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Metrics 3, 4 and 5. A handful of CSRF mismatches is normal — a stale tab, a form left open over lunch; a run of them is either an attack or a deploy that changed the token contract and broke every open session, and the first thing to check is which.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Logs",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Errors and warnings, all services",
      "type": "logs",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${DS_LOKI}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${DS_LOKI}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{container=~\".+\", level=~\"(?i)error|fatal|severe|warn|warning\"}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "One query across every container, which is only possible because Promtail extracts a severity label from both shapes of log this platform produces: parsed JSON fields from the services this project controls, and a regex over the conventional level words for Alfresco, ActiveMQ and Solr, which write plain text and were never going to agree on a format.",
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false
      }
    }
  ]
}
